<Base title="About" description="What APAC DC Wire tracks and how it works">
  <article class="about">
    <h1>About APAC DC Wire</h1>

    <p>
      APAC DC Wire is a daily, automated digest of data center industry news across
      Asia-Pacific. It tracks announcements about hyperscale and colocation campuses,
      capacity expansions, power and land deals, regulation, and the AI infrastructure
      build-out reshaping the region.
    </p>

    <h2>What we track</h2>
    <p>Coverage is organized into five APAC regions, plus a Global bucket:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>China</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Japan</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Korea</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Australia</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Southeast Asia</strong> — Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Thailand, Vietnam, the Philippines, and neighbors</li>
      <li><strong>Global</strong> — stories outside the region that materially affect APAC, such as GPU supply or global cloud capex</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      An automated pipeline polls industry publications and news feeds every day, then an
      AI pipeline clusters duplicate coverage of the same story, scores each story for
      relevance and importance (0–100), and writes the summaries and "why it matters"
      notes you see on the homepage. The result is published as one JSON file per day and
      rendered into this static site.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources and attribution</h2>
    <p>
      Every story credits the publications that reported it, with direct links to the
      original articles. The "heat" number on trending stories is simply the count of
      distinct sources covering the same story.
    </p>

    <h2>A note on scores</h2>
    <p>
      Scores, summaries, and "why it matters" notes are AI-generated heuristics designed
      to help you skim — they are not editorial judgment, investment advice, or a
      substitute for reading the original reporting. Always follow the source links for
      the full picture.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
